<% content_for :title, "About" %>
<% content_for :analytics, "on" %>
<% page_meta description: "Why Shadetree exists, who builds it, and the promises it keeps to small service businesses." %>

<section class="border-b border-line">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.04em] text-ink sm:text-5xl">Software for the crews who keep neighborhoods running.</h1>
    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-subtle">
      <p>Most small service businesses still quote by text message, paper or a word-processor template. Approvals get lost, the schedule lives on a whiteboard, and invoices go out late, often on a Sunday night.</p>
      <p>The tools that fix this were built for bigger companies. They mostly charge by the seat, take an afternoon to set up, and assume an office.</p>
      <p>Shadetree is built for the owner who also does the work: one to ten people, running the day from a phone. It does the part of the day that makes money, from the first request to getting paid, and tries to do that part very well.</p>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bg-canvas" aria-labelledby="promises-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
    <h2 id="promises-heading" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">What we promise</h2>
    <dl class="mt-10 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-8 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <% [ [ "Clients never need an account", "Every quote, visit and invoice opens from a secure link. Nothing for your clients to download or remember." ],
           [ "Honest pricing", "Free to start, and paid plans priced by how many quotes you send. Hitting a limit never breaks something a client is already doing." ],
           [ "Your data is yours", "Export your clients, quotes, jobs and invoices whenever you like, on any plan." ],
           [ "Your brand, not ours", "Clients see your name, logo and colors on every page and email." ],
           [ "Fewer features, finished", "We'd rather make the core work fast and reliable than add screens nobody asked for." ],
           [ "Made for phones", "Every page is built to be quick on an ordinary phone with a patchy signal." ] ].each do |title, text| %>
        <div class="border-t border-line pt-5"><dt class="font-bold text-ink"><%= title %></dt><dd class="mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-subtle"><%= text %></dd></div>
      <% end %>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="who-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
    <h2 id="who-heading" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">Who builds it</h2>
    <div id="founder-story" class="mt-5 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-subtle">
      <p>I'm Ryan Tulino. I spent my twenties in home services: cleaning carpets, moving, landscaping, lawn care, pest control, painting and construction. Then I switched to tech.</p>
      <p>I'm handy and fix most things around the house myself, and a lot of my family runs home service businesses. So I know the work, and the people who do it.</p>
      <p>I believe the back office should fit around the work instead of getting in its way, and that clients deserve the best possible experience. It should be easy for them to know when the work is scheduled, what's getting done, and how much it's going to cost.</p>
      <p>Transparency is a first principle for me, and for Shadetree.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <%= link_to "Get in touch", contact_path, class: button_classes(:secondary, :lg) %>
      <%= link_to "Start free", new_user_registration_path, class: button_classes(:primary, :lg) %>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
